B. Cloud flow is incorrect because a flow is an automation artifact, not a Dataverse message contract. A flow can call Dataverse or respond to Dataverse events, but it is not the primary implementation approach for exposing a reusable operation in the Dataverse API itself. It also introduces different execution characteristics than a native message. So it misses the architectural requirement being tested.

C. JavaScript web resource is incorrect because JavaScript web resources are attached to client events in model-driven apps and operate in the user session. They are appropriate for form behavior, command interactions, and UI automation, but not for defining a reusable Dataverse message callable across server-side components and flows. Using JavaScript here would couple the logic to the client channel. That fails the component design requirement.

