C. Shared mailbox owner + basic auth connector is incorrect because a shared mailbox is not the right identity model for owning and running enterprise Power Automate flows. Basic authentication is also weaker and does not meet the stated Entra ID requirement for the API. Even if the connector could technically connect, the design would still be misaligned with lifecycle resilience and modern auth expectations. It is a workaround, not the right architecture.

D. Personal flow owner + environment variable secret is incorrect because environment variables help with configuration portability, not with selecting the correct ownership and authentication model by themselves. Keeping the flow owned by a person reintroduces operational fragility. It also still leaves the design centered on secret management rather than using Entra ID as the actual authentication mechanism. The option improves deployment hygiene but not the core authn/authz design.

