D. Out-of-box activity table is incorrect because activity tables are meant for activity-centric business records such as appointments, tasks, emails, and related work items. Telemetry data is not activity-shaped in that sense, and the scenario’s primary challenge is scale and throughput. Choosing an activity table would confuse business semantics with storage architecture. It is not a realistic fit for this workload.

