• B. CreateRequest with source GUID. The scenario does not know the Dataverse GUID, and Microsoft notes that alternate keys are the common identity mechanism for this class of integration. A create-only request would also fail the insert-or-update requirement because it does not handle existing records cleanly. This option confuses record creation with keyed synchronization.



• C. ExecuteMultipleRequest batch. Batching is about packaging multiple operations, not about selecting create-versus-update semantics for a single keyed row. It does not replace the insert-or-update decision logic that UpsertRequest provides. This distractor sounds performance-oriented, but it does not solve the actual behavior requirement.

